  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "1 Chronicles",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 17,
    "summary": "Nathan first approves David’s building of a house of the Lord, then restrains him—David’s son will build the temple—The triumph of Israel is foretold—David thanks the Lord for His goodness to Israel.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Now it came to pass, as David sat in his house, that David said to Nathan the prophet, Lo, I dwell in an house of cedars, but the ark of the covenant of the Lord remaineth under curtains.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 162,
            "end": 171
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:1",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Nathan said unto David, Do all that is in thine heart; for God is with thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 43
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:2",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass the same night, that the word of God came to Nathan, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:3",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Go and tell David my servant, Thus saith the Lord, Thou shalt not build me an house to dwell in:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:4",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "For I have not dwelt in an house since the day that I brought up Israel unto this day; but have gone from tent to tent, and from one tabernacle to another.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 132
          },
          {
            "start": 144,
            "end": 155
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:5",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Wheresoever I have walked with all Israel, spake I a word to any of the judges of Israel, whom I commanded to feed my people, saying, Why have ye not built me an house of cedars?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 162,
            "end": 167,
            "text": "2 Sam. 7:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Sam. 7:7.",
            "prettyString": "2 Samuel 7:7",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2samuel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 7,
                    "end": 7,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 7,
                        "end": 7
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:6",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Now therefore thus shalt thou say unto my servant David, Thus saith the Lord of hosts, I took thee from the sheepcote, even from following the sheep, that thou shouldest be ruler over my people Israel:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 119,
            "end": 123
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:7",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And I have been with thee whithersoever thou hast walked, and have cut off all thine enemies from before thee, and have made thee a name like the name of the great men that are in the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 173,
            "end": 176
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:8",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Also I will ordain a place for my people Israel, and will plant them, and they shall dwell in their place, and shall be moved no more; neither shall the children of wickedness waste them any more, as at the beginning,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:9",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And since the time that I commanded judges to be over my people Israel. Moreover I will subdue all thine enemies. Furthermore I tell thee that the Lord will build thee an house.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "Ps. 89:10; Micah 4:10; D&C 65:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 89:10; Micah 4:10; D&C 65:6.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 89:10; Micah 4:10; D&C 65:6",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 89,
                    "end": 89,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 10,
                        "end": 10
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "micah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 4,
                    "end": 4,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 10,
                        "end": 10
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "doctrineandcovenants",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 65,
                    "end": 65,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 6,
                        "end": 6
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:10",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And it shall come to pass, when thy days be expired that thou must go to be with thy fathers, that I will raise up thy seed after thee, which shall be of thy sons; and I will establish his kingdom.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:11",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall build me an house, and I will stablish his throne for ever.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:12",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "I will be his father, and he shall be my son: and I will not take my mercy away from him, as I took it from him that was before thee:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "Heb. 1:5 (5–6)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 102
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 111
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:13",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "But I will settle him in mine house and in my kingdom for ever: and his throne shall be established for evermore.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "Jer. 23:11; D&C 124:145."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jer. 23:11; D&C 124:145.",
            "prettyString": "Jeremiah 23:11; D&C 124:145",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jeremiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 23,
                    "end": 23,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 11,
                        "end": 11
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "doctrineandcovenants",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 124,
                    "end": 124,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 145,
                        "end": 145
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:14",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so did Nathan speak unto David.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:15",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And David the king came and sat before the Lord, and said, Who am I, O Lord God, and what is mine house, that thou hast brought me hitherto?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 65
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 92
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:16",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And yet this was a small thing in thine eyes, O God; for thou hast also spoken of thy servant’s house for a great while to come, and hast regarded me according to the estate of a man of high degree, O Lord God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 7
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:17",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "What can David speak more to thee for the honour of thy servant? for thou knowest thy servant.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:18",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "O Lord, for thy servant’s sake, and according to thine own heart, hast thou done all this greatness, in making known all these great things.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "2 Sam. 7:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 126
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Sam. 7:21.",
            "prettyString": "2 Samuel 7:21",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2samuel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 7,
                    "end": 7,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 21,
                        "end": 21
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:19",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "O Lord, there is none like thee, neither is there any God beside thee, according to all that we have heard with our ears.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:20",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And what one nation in the earth is like thy people Israel, whom God went to redeem to be his own people, to make thee a name of greatness and terribleness, by driving out nations from before thy people, whom thou hast redeemed out of Egypt?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 35
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 89
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:21",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "For thy people Israel didst thou make thine own people for ever; and thou, Lord, becamest their God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:22",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore now, Lord, let the thing that thou hast spoken concerning thy servant and concerning his house be established for ever, and do as thou hast said.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:23",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Let it even be established, that thy name may be magnified for ever, saying, The Lord of hosts is the God of Israel, even a God to Israel: and let the house of David thy servant be established before thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 97
          },
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 121
          },
          {
            "start": 143,
            "end": 146
          },
          {
            "start": 178,
            "end": 180
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:24",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "For thou, O my God, hast told thy servant that thou wilt build him an house: therefore thy servant hath found in his heart to pray before thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 122
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:25",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, Lord, thou art God, and hast promised this goodness unto thy servant:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:26",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Now therefore let it please thee to bless the house of thy servant, that it may be before thee for ever: for thou blessest, O Lord, and it shall be blessed for ever.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 147
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 17:27",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 27
      }
    ]
  },
